s :bthe Texas victory that changed American history /cBrian Kilmeade.30aTexas victory that changed American history14aSam Houston & the Alamo avengers 1a[New York] :bSentinel,c[2019]  a272 pages, 16 unnumbered unnumbered leaves of plates :billustrations (some color), maps ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  mGender group:ngdraMen2lcdgt  mNationality/regional group:nnataNew Yorkers (New York State)2lcdgt  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  aMaps on endpapers.00tPrologue: The lessons of battle --tGeneral Jackson's Protégé --tGone to Texas --t"Come and Take It" --tConcepción --tA Slow Siege at the Alamo --tThe Defenders --tTwelve Days of Uncertainty --tThe Massacre --tBring Out the Dead --tHouston Hears the News --tFort Defiance --tThe Texian Exodus --tAn Army Assembles --tThe Battle at San Jacinto --t"Remember the Alamo!" --tOld Sam Jacinto --tPresident Sam Houston --tEpilogue: The Founding and the Founders of Texas.  aMarch 1836: The story of the Alamo is familiar to most: more than two hundred Texians trapped in an adobe mission, and massacred. Though the rallying cry of "Remember the Alamo" rang across the country, Houston knew it was poor strategy to aggressively retaliate immediately. One month after the massacre, he and his army of underdog Texians soundly defeated Santa Anna's troops in under eighteen minutes at the Battle of San Jacinto, and in doing so won the independence for which so many had died. Kilmeade brings one of the most pivotal moments in American history to life. -- adapted from jacket  aIngrambShelf ready books10aHouston, Sam,d1793-1863.10aSanta Anna, Antonio López de,d1794-1876. 0aTexasxHistoryyRevolution, 1835-1836. 0aSan Jacinto, Battle of, Tex., 1836. 0aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.)xSiege, 1836. 0aGovernorszTexasvBiography. 0aLegislatorszUnited StatesvBiography. 0aTexasxHistoryyTo 1846. 1aTexas 1aTexaszSan Antonio. 1aTexasxHistory. 7aHISTORYzUnited Statesx19th Century. 7aUnited StatesxHistoryxState & LocalxSouthwest (AZ, NM, OK, TX) 7aLegislators. 7aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.), Battle of the, 1836. 7aBattle of San Jacintoc(Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01404392 7aRevolutionc(Texas :d1835-1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01354582 7aSiege of Alamoc(San Antonio, Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01910462 7aTo 18462fast 7aBiographies.08iOnline version:aKilmeade, Brian.tSam Houston and the Alamo avengers.dNew York : Sentinel, 2019z9780525540564w(DLC)  2019022818  a92bTNTffaF390 .H84 K55 2019wLCc1i50706010953454f6/2/2025g2lSTACKSmERCp$28.00rYsYtBOOKu3/19/2021xBOOK00847cam a2200265   4500001000800000003000600008005001700014008004100031040003000072020001800102020001500120035002200135050002200157049000900179100001700188245006000205260003600265300002300301590003000324650002300354650003800377650002300415994001200438945013100450u581759SIRSI20210613042801.5200817s2020    xx            000 0 eng d  aTOHbengcTOHdJCHdOCLCO  a9780062999719  a0062999710  a(OCoLC)1192354301 0aKF4772b.C67 2020  aMAIN1 aCose, Ellis.10aShort Life and Curious Death of Free Speech in America.  bHarperCollins Publishersc2020.  a208 pages.;c23 cm  aIngrambShelf ready books 0aPolitical culture. 0aFreedom of speechzUnited States. 7aFreedom of speech.  a92bTNTffaKF4772 .C67 2020wLCc1i50706010960863d3/25/2022e3/9/2022f6/4/2025g3lSTACKSmERCn2p$23.99rYsYtBOOKu6/14/2021xBOOK01417cam a2200409   u591049SIRSI20211006213032.0181009s2019    cau           000 0 eng    a  2018045903  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdJCHdOCLCOdOCL  a9781684126590q(hardcover)  a1684126592  a(OCoLC)105724220500aPR6019.O9bA6 2019  aMAIN1 aJoyce, James,d1882-1941,eauthor.10aWorks.kSelections10aDubliners & A portrait of the artist as a young man and other works /cJames Joyce.3 aDubliners and A 