ring Out the Dead --tHouston Hears the News --tFort Defiance --tThe Texian Exodus --tAn Army Assembles --tThe Battle at San Jacinto --t"Remember the Alamo!" --tOld Sam Jacinto --tPresident Sam Houston --tEpilogue: The Founding and the Founders of Texas.  aMarch 1836: The story of the Alamo is familiar to most: more than two hundred Texians trapped in an adobe mission, and massacred. Though the rallying cry of "Remember the Alamo" rang across the country, Houston knew it was poor strategy to aggressively retaliate immediately. One month after the massacre, he and his army of underdog Texians soundly defeated Santa Anna's troops in under eighteen minutes at the Battle of San Jacinto, and in doing so won the independence for which so many had died. Kilmeade brings one of the most pivotal moments in American history to life. -- adapted from jacket  aIngrambShelf ready books10aHouston, Sam,d1793-1863.10aSanta Anna, Antonio López de,d1794-1876. 0aTexasxHistoryyRevolution, 1835-1836. 0aSan Jacinto, Battle of, Tex., 1836. 0aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.)xSiege, 1836. 0aGovernorszTexasvBiography. 0aLegislatorszUnited StatesvBiography. 0aTexasxHistoryyTo 1846. 1aTexas 1aTexaszSan Antonio. 1aTexasxHistory. 7aHISTORYzUnited Statesx19th Century. 7aUnited StatesxHistoryxState & LocalxSouthwest (AZ, NM, OK, TX) 7aLegislators. 7aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.), Battle of the, 1836. 7aBattle of San Jacintoc(Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01404392 7aRevolutionc(Texas :d1835-1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01354582 7aSiege of Alamoc(San Antonio, Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01910462 7aTo 18462fast 7aBiographies.08iOnline version:aKilmeade, Brian.tSam Houston and the Alamo avengers.dNew York : Sentinel, 2019z9780525540564w(DLC)  2019022818  a92bTNTffaF390 .H84 K55 2019wLCc1i50706010953454f6/2/2025g2lSTACKSmERCp$28.00rYsYtBOOKu3/19/2021xBOOK00847cam a2200265   450000100080000000300060000800500170001